Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:36:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/8] collab-web: interface scale control

Every shell size is a hardcoded px value, so there was no way to make the
UI readable on a phone. A root font size cannot help those values, so the
app frame takes `zoom` instead: unlike `transform: scale` it participates
in layout, so rows still shrink and ellipsize at the scaled width.

`height` is evaluated in the pre-zoom coordinate space, so the frame
divides the viewport height by the scale and stays exactly one viewport
tall at any setting. The preference persists in localStorage beside the
theme.

(cherry picked from commit 4dddddd7e278c7d6c124dd31047de4dbcabcf816)
